@startsalt
' Screen: Rubric Disagreement Analytics
' User Stories:
'   - As a test engineer, I can compare rubric versions A/B to detect scoring drift
'   - As a test engineer, I can see disagreement rate and Cohen's Kappa at a glance
'   - As a test engineer, I can view a confusion matrix to understand error patterns
'   - As a test engineer, I can drill into specific steps where versions disagree
'   - As a test engineer, I can export disagreement data for offline analysis

{
  {
    <b>codefre.sh</b> | Scripts | Prompts | Rubrics | Personas | Runs | Settings
  }
  ==
  {
    <b>Rubric Disagreement Analytics</b> | [Export CSV] | [< Back]
  }
  ==
  {
    <b>Comparison Configuration</b>
    --
    Script        | ^checkout-flow-v2^
    Rubric A      | ^RAG Faithfulness — v2^
    Rubric B      | ^RAG Faithfulness — v3^
    Time Range    | ^Last 30 days^       | [Recalculate]
  }
  --
  {
    {+
      <b>Disagreement Rate</b>
      ==
      <b>12.3%</b>
      <i>47 of 382 steps</i>
    }
    |
    {+
      <b>Cohen's Kappa</b>
      ==
      <b>0.74</b>
      <i>Substantial agreement</i>
    }
    |
    {+
      <b>Avg Score Delta</b>
      ==
      <b>+0.42</b>
      <i>v3 scores higher on avg</i>
    }
    |
    {+
      <b>Steps Evaluated</b>
      ==
      <b>382</b>
      <i>across 14 run sessions</i>
    }
  }
  --
  {
    {
      <b>Confusion Matrix</b> <i>(rows = v2, cols = v3)</i>
      --
      {#
        <b>v2 \\ v3</b> | <b>Pass</b> | <b>Warn</b> | <b>Fail</b>
        <b>Pass</b>     | 201    |  18    |   3
        <b>Warn</b>     |  19    |  98    |   7
        <b>Fail</b>     |   2    |   9    |  25
      }
      " "
      <i>Diagonal = agreement. Off-diagonal = disagreement.</i>
      <i>Upper triangle = v3 more lenient than v2.</i>
      <i>Lower triangle = v3 more strict than v2.</i>
    }
    |
    {
      <b>Disagreement Trend</b> <i>(30-day, by week)</i>
